WEBVTT

00:00:08.926 --> 00:00:10.553
Report.

00:00:10.594 --> 00:00:14.360
There's an object of some kind
closing in on our position.

00:00:14.398 --> 00:00:15.797
On screen.

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:19.868
It appears
to be an unmanned probe.

00:00:19.903 --> 00:00:22.497
Approximately one-half
meter in diameter.

00:00:22.539 --> 00:00:24.734
There are
no identifiable armaments.

00:00:24.775 --> 00:00:27.209
Captain, we are being...

00:00:27.244 --> 00:00:29.712
you are being hailed, by name.

00:00:29.746 --> 00:00:32.374
Open a channel.

00:00:32.416 --> 00:00:35.442
This is Captain
Jean-Luc Picard of...

00:00:35.485 --> 00:00:37.043
Captain, I am reading
a power surge.

00:00:37.087 --> 00:00:38.645
Shields up.

00:00:41.191 --> 00:00:45.719
The beam appears to contain
holographic imaging information.

00:00:45.762 --> 00:00:47.855
It's trying
to project something.

00:00:47.898 --> 00:00:49.229
Isolate the bandwidth.

00:00:49.266 --> 00:00:51.700
Let the signal
through the shields.

00:00:54.972 --> 00:00:57.099
Bok.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.165
I trust you remember me, Picard

00:00:59.209 --> 00:01:01.234
because I haven't forgotten you

00:01:01.278 --> 00:01:03.007
or how you murdered my son.

00:01:03.046 --> 00:01:05.037
For 15 years now, I've thought

00:01:05.082 --> 00:01:08.848
about how to avenge his death,
but nothing I could do to you

00:01:08.885 --> 00:01:11.615
could equal what you did to me...
until now.

00:01:11.655 --> 00:01:14.089
You thought
you could hide him from me

00:01:14.124 --> 00:01:15.318
didn't you?

00:01:15.359 --> 00:01:16.986
But I found out about him.

00:01:17.027 --> 00:01:19.996
Jason Vigo is as good as dead.

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:22.726
I'm going to kill your son,
Picard

00:01:22.766 --> 00:01:25.394
just like you killed mine.

00:02:01.104 --> 00:02:05.438
Space, the final frontier.

00:02:05.475 --> 00:02:09.309
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:02:09.346 --> 00:02:11.314
Its continuing mission...

00:02:11.348 --> 00:02:15.284
to explore strange new worlds

00:02:15.318 --> 00:02:19.755
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:24.659
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:03:22.686 --> 00:03:25.086
Mr. Worf, put a tractor beam
on that probe.

00:03:25.122 --> 00:03:27.886
Determine if it's safe
to beam it on board.

00:03:27.958 --> 00:03:30.426
I want to know
where it came from.

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:34.419
Mr. Data, see if there is
any mention of a Jason Vigo

00:03:34.464 --> 00:03:35.897
in Federation records.

00:03:35.966 --> 00:03:39.902
You might start
with Miranda Vigo.

00:03:40.003 --> 00:03:42.767
She was born on New Gaul
about 50 years ago.

00:03:42.806 --> 00:03:44.467
Aye, sir.

00:03:44.508 --> 00:03:47.306
Number One,
contact the Ferengi government.

00:03:47.344 --> 00:03:49.369
Find out all you can about Bok.

00:03:49.412 --> 00:03:51.073
He was wearing
a DaiMon's uniform.

00:03:51.114 --> 00:03:53.605
If he has regained his rank,
I want to know why.

00:04:04.828 --> 00:04:06.295
Come.

00:04:06.329 --> 00:04:07.660
The Ferengi government

00:04:07.697 --> 00:04:10.860
is debating an amendment
to the Rules of Acquisition.

00:04:10.967 --> 00:04:13.731
It could be a while
before we hear from them.

00:04:16.573 --> 00:04:19.701
Data found out
that the woman you mentioned

00:04:19.743 --> 00:04:21.711
has a son named Jason.

00:04:21.745 --> 00:04:25.579
This is the most recent picture
we could find.

00:04:31.421 --> 00:04:32.752
How old is the boy now?

00:04:32.789 --> 00:04:34.086
Twenty-three.

00:04:34.124 --> 00:04:37.321
He and his mother left Earth
12 years ago.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.385
They settled on Camor V.

00:04:39.429 --> 00:04:40.896
That's all we know.

00:04:40.964 --> 00:04:44.661
The planet's records
are virtually nonexistent.

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:45.998
Picard to Bridge.

00:04:46.036 --> 00:04:49.528
Set a course
for the Camor system, warp five.

00:04:49.573 --> 00:04:51.063
Aye, sir.

00:04:53.743 --> 00:04:55.574
Will...

00:04:56.846 --> 00:04:59.474
I do appreciate your not asking

00:04:59.516 --> 00:05:02.849
but I do think
that you have a right to know.

00:05:02.953 --> 00:05:06.753
There is a possibility
that the boy is my son.

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:13.423
I was involved with his mother
for a short time about...

00:05:13.463 --> 00:05:16.432
well, 24 years ago.

00:05:16.466 --> 00:05:18.593
We met through a friend

00:05:18.635 --> 00:05:21.536
when I was on shore leave
on Earth.

00:05:21.571 --> 00:05:26.702
It was, uh... all very romantic,
very intense

00:05:26.743 --> 00:05:28.836
probably because we both knew

00:05:28.878 --> 00:05:31.540
that I would be leaving
in two weeks

00:05:31.581 --> 00:05:34.550
and we kept in touch for a while

00:05:34.584 --> 00:05:38.748
but we never managed
to get together again.

00:05:38.788 --> 00:05:41.018
She never said anything to you
about being pregnant?

00:05:42.892 --> 00:05:44.189
No.

00:05:44.227 --> 00:05:48.027
So either Bok is wrong,
and I'm not the father

00:05:48.064 --> 00:05:51.693
or Miranda decided
to raise the child alone

00:05:51.735 --> 00:05:54.704
which, quite frankly,
wouldn't surprise me.

00:05:54.738 --> 00:05:58.538
She was very independent...

00:05:58.575 --> 00:06:00.543
very strong-willed.

00:06:00.577 --> 00:06:04.206
She would have to be
to get by on Camor V.

00:06:04.247 --> 00:06:07.683
But whether he's my son or not,
he is in danger.

00:06:07.717 --> 00:06:11.483
Bok tried to kill me six years
ago and I don't doubt

00:06:11.521 --> 00:06:15.685
that he will try to make good
his threat against the boy.

00:06:23.566 --> 00:06:24.794
Anything?

00:06:24.834 --> 00:06:27.826
There are no Ferengi vessels
within range of our scanners.

00:06:27.871 --> 00:06:30.135
Captain, I am unable
to find any information

00:06:30.173 --> 00:06:32.038
on Jason Vigo's
current whereabouts.

00:06:32.075 --> 00:06:33.542
What about his mother?

00:06:33.576 --> 00:06:34.873
No, sir.

00:06:34.911 --> 00:06:36.879
Miranda was trained
as a botanist.

00:06:36.913 --> 00:06:39.882
She always used to talk
about running a farm one day.

00:06:39.916 --> 00:06:42.510
Maybe we should concentrate
on the agricultural areas.

00:06:42.552 --> 00:06:44.645
That would significantly
narrow our search.

00:06:44.688 --> 00:06:47.179
The only cultivated land is
on the southern continent

00:06:47.223 --> 00:06:49.214
and there are relatively
few people engaged

00:06:49.259 --> 00:06:50.556
in agricultural activities.

00:06:50.593 --> 00:06:53.528
There cannot be many
non-Camorites among them.

00:06:53.563 --> 00:06:56.054
Scan for human life signs.

00:06:56.099 --> 00:06:59.068
I am detecting eight humans.

00:06:59.102 --> 00:07:01.332
Three are female.

00:07:01.371 --> 00:07:04.135
However, they are all too young
to be Miranda Vigo.

00:07:04.174 --> 00:07:05.641
What about males?

00:07:05.675 --> 00:07:08.473
One is an infant.

00:07:08.511 --> 00:07:10.809
Another is elderly.

00:07:10.847 --> 00:07:12.712
Two are middle-aged.

00:07:12.749 --> 00:07:14.944
That's seven.
You said there were eight.

00:07:14.984 --> 00:07:18.681
I am having difficulty getting
a clear reading on the eighth.

00:07:18.722 --> 00:07:22.214
The individual appears to be
approximately two kilometers

00:07:22.258 --> 00:07:24.317
beneath the planet's surface.

00:07:24.361 --> 00:07:25.555
Male or female?

00:07:25.595 --> 00:07:26.857
Male.

00:07:26.896 --> 00:07:28.659
Between 20 and 30 years old.

00:07:28.698 --> 00:07:30.222
No one in their right mind

00:07:30.266 --> 00:07:32.496
would go that far
underground alone.

00:07:32.535 --> 00:07:34.025
Unless he were forced to.

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:36.664
Captain, I am reading seismic
instability in the area.

00:07:36.706 --> 00:07:38.071
He is in danger.

00:07:38.108 --> 00:07:41.305
Relay his coordinates
to the transporter room.

00:07:41.344 --> 00:07:43.209
Have them beam him aboard.

00:07:43.246 --> 00:07:44.736
Aye, sir.

00:07:54.257 --> 00:07:56.248
What the...?

00:07:59.896 --> 00:08:01.864
This is a Federation ship.

00:08:01.898 --> 00:08:03.058
That's right.

00:08:03.099 --> 00:08:05.397
I'm Captain Picard,
Jean-Luc Picard.

00:08:05.435 --> 00:08:08.836
I realize I wasn't supposed
to be spelunking that cave

00:08:08.938 --> 00:08:11.634
but don't you have
something better to do?

00:08:11.674 --> 00:08:13.369
We thought you were at risk.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:14.536
Oh. Well, I wasn't.

00:08:14.577 --> 00:08:17.569
So maybe you should just beam me
back where I was.

00:08:17.614 --> 00:08:19.411
Are you Jason Vigo?

00:08:19.449 --> 00:08:21.849
I, uh...

00:08:21.951 --> 00:08:23.816
I know him.

00:08:23.853 --> 00:08:25.480
Is he in trouble?

00:08:25.522 --> 00:08:27.513
In a manner of speaking.

00:08:28.892 --> 00:08:32.259
Someone has made a threat
against his life.

00:08:34.431 --> 00:08:37.798
Jason, I'm an old friend
of your mother's.

00:08:37.834 --> 00:08:40.530
I'm here
because you're in danger.

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:44.199
Why would anybody
want to kill me?

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:47.767
The person who has made
the threat

00:08:47.811 --> 00:08:51.474
is under the impression
that you...

00:08:51.514 --> 00:08:53.505
are my son.

00:08:55.652 --> 00:08:57.119
Am I?

00:08:58.588 --> 00:09:00.647
I don't know.

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:04.456
My mother never told me
who my father was...

00:09:04.494 --> 00:09:07.258
just that he was in Starfleet.

00:09:07.297 --> 00:09:09.094
Maybe we should contact her.

00:09:09.132 --> 00:09:13.694
She, uh... she died
a few years ago.

00:09:15.371 --> 00:09:17.362
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:09:19.642 --> 00:09:21.837
Jason, I think it's important

00:09:21.878 --> 00:09:24.676
that we find out
one way or the other.

00:09:24.714 --> 00:09:28.172
Would you be willing
to permit a genetic test?

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:31.414
If I'm not your son

00:09:31.454 --> 00:09:34.423
is this person still
going to want to kill me?

00:09:34.457 --> 00:09:35.822
I doubt it.

00:09:35.859 --> 00:09:38.293
In that case, you
won't mind my saying

00:09:38.328 --> 00:09:40.489
that I hope you're
not my father.

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:03.048
What were you doing
in the caves, Jason?

00:10:03.086 --> 00:10:04.713
Are you a seismologist?

00:10:04.754 --> 00:10:06.881
No, I just enjoy climbing.

00:10:06.923 --> 00:10:09.892
Without an antigrav harness?

00:10:09.926 --> 00:10:12.258
No, they get in the way.

00:10:15.098 --> 00:10:17.896
So, what do you do?

00:10:17.934 --> 00:10:21.927
Um... I'm between jobs
right now.

00:10:25.108 --> 00:10:26.598
I see.

00:10:27.777 --> 00:10:29.244
Excuse me, gentlemen.

00:10:29.279 --> 00:10:33.841
The test results are ready
if you'd like to hear them.

00:10:35.285 --> 00:10:39.051
Your genetic code
is a cross between the DNA

00:10:39.088 --> 00:10:42.524
of your mother Miranda Vigo
and your father

00:10:42.559 --> 00:10:45.050
Jean-Luc Picard.

00:11:07.216 --> 00:11:09.309
What's all this?

00:11:09.352 --> 00:11:12.879
Oh, these are
archaeological fragments

00:11:12.922 --> 00:11:15.789
that I've collected
over the years.

00:11:15.825 --> 00:11:18.089
This is a Silvan glyph stone.

00:11:19.962 --> 00:11:23.329
And, um, this is...

00:11:23.366 --> 00:11:25.994
this is a Gorlan prayer stick.

00:11:26.035 --> 00:11:28.526
It's really quite rare.

00:11:28.571 --> 00:11:30.596
Is it valuable?

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:32.608
Oh, not really.

00:11:32.642 --> 00:11:35.839
Only to students
of archaeology such as myself.

00:11:35.878 --> 00:11:39.041
Though, I did have
to hand over a bottle

00:11:39.082 --> 00:11:41.346
of very old Saurian brandy
for it.

00:11:41.384 --> 00:11:43.682
I'd say you got taken.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:46.780
Well, perhaps

00:11:46.823 --> 00:11:50.623
but it's of value
to me nonetheless.

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:54.756
On Camor, something has value
if you can eat it or sell it.

00:11:54.797 --> 00:11:58.130
Everything else is luxury.

00:11:58.167 --> 00:12:00.328
Would you like some tea?

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:02.361
No... thanks.

00:12:03.606 --> 00:12:05.972
Something else?

00:12:06.008 --> 00:12:07.532
No.

00:12:07.577 --> 00:12:10.307
Tea, Earl Grey, hot.

00:12:10.346 --> 00:12:12.405
I'm sure that this whole thing

00:12:12.448 --> 00:12:16.817
is as much of a surprise
to you as it is to me.

00:12:16.853 --> 00:12:21.187
I really want
to be honest with you, Jason.

00:12:21.224 --> 00:12:25.854
I only knew your mother
for a very short time.

00:12:25.895 --> 00:12:29.387
I would have liked
to have known her better...

00:12:31.467 --> 00:12:34.129
it just didn't
work out that way.

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:37.833
You look a lot like her,
you know.

00:12:37.874 --> 00:12:40.035
It's the eyes, I think.

00:12:40.076 --> 00:12:44.604
I would like
to make one thing clear, Jason.

00:12:44.647 --> 00:12:47.912
Your mother never told me
about you.

00:12:47.984 --> 00:12:52.182
If she had, I would have been
part of your life.

00:12:52.221 --> 00:12:54.746
Maybe that's not
what she wanted.

00:12:58.494 --> 00:13:02.191
I think I'd like to go back
to the surface now.

00:13:04.567 --> 00:13:05.864
I think it would be better

00:13:05.902 --> 00:13:07.494
if you stayed on board
the Enterprise

00:13:07.537 --> 00:13:09.596
until we have resolved
this situation with Bok.

00:13:09.639 --> 00:13:12.039
What is this situation
with Bok, anyway?

00:13:12.074 --> 00:13:14.065
I mean,
why does he want me dead?

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:18.740
Years ago, I was forced
to destroy a starship

00:13:18.781 --> 00:13:21.181
commanded by his son.

00:13:21.217 --> 00:13:24.186
Bok apparently feels that it
would be fitting vengeance

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:26.051
to kill my son.

00:13:26.088 --> 00:13:29.546
Well, I can't hide forever.

00:13:29.592 --> 00:13:30.559
Of course not.

00:13:30.593 --> 00:13:32.288
We are trying to locate Bok now.

00:13:32.328 --> 00:13:34.523
I want to confront him,
settle this matter.

00:13:34.564 --> 00:13:37.624
How long is this going to take?

00:13:37.667 --> 00:13:40.761
I assure you,
there is no one more eager

00:13:40.803 --> 00:13:43.465
to put this behind us
than I am.

00:13:50.746 --> 00:13:52.714
Where do I stay?

00:13:52.748 --> 00:13:54.875
We'll get you some quarters.

00:13:57.553 --> 00:13:59.521
Okay, let's go.

00:13:59.555 --> 00:14:02.547
Jason...

00:14:02.592 --> 00:14:04.389
your being here

00:14:04.427 --> 00:14:07.055
I hope it will give us
the chance

00:14:07.096 --> 00:14:09.530
to get to know each other.

00:14:13.002 --> 00:14:15.266
We've managed to shut down
the probe's power system

00:14:15.304 --> 00:14:16.396
so we can beam it aboard

00:14:16.439 --> 00:14:17.770
but It's not going to be easy

00:14:17.807 --> 00:14:19.638
to figure out where
this thing came from.

00:14:19.675 --> 00:14:20.699
Bok took the precaution

00:14:20.743 --> 00:14:22.472
of encrypting the probe's
navigational systems

00:14:22.512 --> 00:14:24.639
so that we would be unable
to decipher its flight path.

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:27.308
We ran an analysis
of the probe's hull.

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:28.874
From the energy signatures

00:14:28.918 --> 00:14:30.545
and the particle
deposits we found

00:14:30.586 --> 00:14:33.384
it looks like it traveled
through a Dichromic Nebula

00:14:33.422 --> 00:14:36.152
was exposed to an intensive
gravimetric distortion

00:14:36.192 --> 00:14:39.093
and passed within one light-year
of a class-4 pulsar.

00:14:39.128 --> 00:14:40.891
Those phenomena
are relatively common.

00:14:40.963 --> 00:14:42.191
We would need to identify

00:14:42.231 --> 00:14:43.823
at least one of them
specifically

00:14:43.866 --> 00:14:45.595
in order to postulate
a flight path.

00:14:45.635 --> 00:14:46.727
Understood.

00:14:46.769 --> 00:14:50.899
Captain, incoming message
from DaiMon Birta.

00:14:50.973 --> 00:14:52.941
Put it on screen.

00:14:54.277 --> 00:14:58.077
Thank you for taking the time
to talk with us, DaiMon.

00:14:58.114 --> 00:15:01.277
I understand you have a problem.

00:15:01.317 --> 00:15:03.148
Yes, it concerns DaiMon Bok.

00:15:03.185 --> 00:15:05.153
Bok is no DaiMon.

00:15:05.187 --> 00:15:07.849
He was relieved of command
six years ago.

00:15:07.957 --> 00:15:11.154
He was unstable, dangerous.

00:15:11.193 --> 00:15:14.185
We had to confine him
to Rog Prison.

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:15.788
But he's no longer there.

00:15:15.831 --> 00:15:19.790
He was able to buy himself out
about two years ago.

00:15:19.835 --> 00:15:21.462
I see.

00:15:21.504 --> 00:15:24.098
Do you know his whereabouts now?

00:15:24.140 --> 00:15:29.578
I understand he was seen
in the Dorias Cluster

00:15:29.612 --> 00:15:30.806
not too long ago.

00:15:30.846 --> 00:15:34.213
But that cluster consists
of more than 20 star systems.

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:40.721
You don't have
to thank me, Captain.

00:15:40.756 --> 00:15:42.485
Believe it or not,
Captain that might

00:15:42.525 --> 00:15:43.992
have given us the fix we need.

00:15:44.026 --> 00:15:45.755
There's a nebula
in the Dorias Cluster

00:15:45.795 --> 00:15:47.660
that matches
the same particle signature

00:15:47.697 --> 00:15:48.721
we found on the probe.

00:15:48.764 --> 00:15:50.061
There is a class-4 pulsar

00:15:50.099 --> 00:15:52.294
three light-years
from the nebula.

00:15:52.335 --> 00:15:56.328
My calculations indicate
the probe was launched

00:15:56.372 --> 00:15:58.499
in the Xendi Sabu system.

00:15:58.541 --> 00:16:00.441
Plot a course,
take us out of orbit.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:16.288
Jean-Luc, come in.

00:16:16.325 --> 00:16:19.817
I think I need to talk
to a parent.

00:16:28.537 --> 00:16:30.402
So, what's he like?

00:16:30.439 --> 00:16:33.408
I'm not sure
that I can tell you.

00:16:33.442 --> 00:16:35.740
He puts up so many barriers.

00:16:35.778 --> 00:16:38.542
I have no idea
what is underneath.

00:16:38.581 --> 00:16:40.014
Keep in mind he's had 20 years

00:16:40.049 --> 00:16:42.017
to be angry
that his father wasn't there.

00:16:42.051 --> 00:16:44.713
It's going to take some time
to get over those feelings

00:16:44.754 --> 00:16:47.348
but I do think it's possible.

00:16:48.591 --> 00:16:49.649
Perhaps.

00:16:49.692 --> 00:16:52.889
But surely it would be wrong
to force the issue.

00:16:52.928 --> 00:16:57.456
My sense is that he is
a very independent young man.

00:16:57.500 --> 00:16:59.900
Perhaps it would be best
if I left him alone.

00:17:00.002 --> 00:17:03.335
Let him come to me
if he wants to.

00:17:05.474 --> 00:17:07.669
Maybe you're right

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:10.838
but I think
you should consider this.

00:17:10.946 --> 00:17:14.177
Are you doing the best thing
for Jason

00:17:14.216 --> 00:17:16.343
or what's easiest for you?

00:17:25.194 --> 00:17:27.719
Yeah.

00:17:29.532 --> 00:17:31.466
Hello, Jason.

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:33.525
I'm Deanna Troi,
Ship's Counselor.

00:17:33.569 --> 00:17:35.230
Come in.

00:17:35.271 --> 00:17:38.399
Did Captain Picard
ask you to come talk to me?

00:17:38.441 --> 00:17:41.342
No, I just thought I'd come
and see how you were doing.

00:17:41.377 --> 00:17:43.436
A lot's happened
in the last few hours.

00:17:43.479 --> 00:17:45.709
I thought you might like
to talk about it.

00:17:45.748 --> 00:17:47.079
I'll be all right.

00:17:47.116 --> 00:17:49.414
People have wanted
to kill me before.

00:17:49.452 --> 00:17:51.750
But you've never met
your father before.

00:17:51.787 --> 00:17:55.086
And I have to admit,
I never thought I would.

00:17:55.124 --> 00:17:58.616
It must be somewhat
overwhelming.

00:17:58.661 --> 00:18:01.255
I'm a little shaky.

00:18:01.297 --> 00:18:02.821
Well, that's only natural.

00:18:02.898 --> 00:18:05.366
But you know what?

00:18:05.401 --> 00:18:08.393
I feel better already
just talking to you.

00:18:08.437 --> 00:18:11.736
So, how did you feel
about the Captain?

00:18:11.774 --> 00:18:13.742
About your father?

00:18:13.776 --> 00:18:15.368
He's okay.

00:18:15.411 --> 00:18:17.379
A little stiff.

00:18:17.413 --> 00:18:19.381
But where are you from?

00:18:19.415 --> 00:18:21.781
I was born on Betazed.

00:18:21.817 --> 00:18:25.776
Do all the women there
have eyes like yours?

00:18:25.821 --> 00:18:28.449
Look, Jason, I came here
to talk to you

00:18:28.491 --> 00:18:30.118
because
I'm the Ship's Counselor.

00:18:30.159 --> 00:18:33.788
If you don't want
to talk to me in that way

00:18:33.829 --> 00:18:35.763
then I think I should go.

00:18:36.799 --> 00:18:38.664
Fine.

00:18:40.569 --> 00:18:42.867
You're welcome
to make an appointment

00:18:42.905 --> 00:18:44.532
to come to my office.

00:18:44.573 --> 00:18:46.438
Maybe I'll do just that.

00:19:03.692 --> 00:19:06.718
Picard, can you hear me?

00:19:11.834 --> 00:19:14.029
I will kill him, Picard

00:19:14.069 --> 00:19:17.266
and there's nothing
you can do about it.

00:19:17.306 --> 00:19:20.070
Security to Captain's quarters
immediately.

00:19:30.852 --> 00:19:31.819
Our shields were up.

00:19:31.853 --> 00:19:33.787
How could he have
beamed through them?

00:19:33.821 --> 00:19:34.845
I'm not sure he did.

00:19:34.889 --> 00:19:37.050
Sensors don't show
any sign of an intruder.

00:19:37.091 --> 00:19:39.423
Could it have been
another hologram?

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:41.428
I don't think so, Captain.

00:19:41.462 --> 00:19:43.692
Something has to generate
a hologram.

00:19:43.731 --> 00:19:45.198
We would have detected it.

00:19:45.233 --> 00:19:47.701
Bok once used
a mind-control device

00:19:47.735 --> 00:19:49.100
to make me hallucinate.

00:19:49.137 --> 00:19:51.605
That device emitted a very
specific energy signature.

00:19:51.639 --> 00:19:53.504
I'm not reading
anything like that.

00:19:53.541 --> 00:19:55.008
Could he have modified
the device

00:19:55.042 --> 00:19:56.873
so he could use it
without being detected?

00:19:56.978 --> 00:19:58.377
It's possible.

00:19:58.413 --> 00:19:59.641
I'll recalibrate the sensors

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:01.409
to scan for low-intensity
transmissions

00:20:01.449 --> 00:20:03.440
and just to be sure,
I'll sweep your quarters

00:20:03.484 --> 00:20:04.610
with a resonance scanner.

00:20:04.652 --> 00:20:07.621
Good. Keep me posted.

00:20:07.655 --> 00:20:11.113
Mr. Worf, I want you to assign
a security detail to Jason.

00:20:11.159 --> 00:20:12.626
And what about yourself?

00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:15.629
I am not the target
of Bok's threats.

00:20:15.663 --> 00:20:17.893
Jason is.

00:20:17.932 --> 00:20:20.901
Captain, I have compiled
all available records

00:20:20.935 --> 00:20:23.529
pertaining to Jason Vigo's
criminal record.

00:20:23.571 --> 00:20:24.538
Criminal record?

00:20:24.572 --> 00:20:26.267
Yes, sir.
He has been charged

00:20:26.307 --> 00:20:29.606
three times with petty theft,
twice for disorderly conduct

00:20:29.644 --> 00:20:32.670
and several dozen times
with trespassing.

00:20:32.713 --> 00:20:34.180
Trespassing?

00:20:34.215 --> 00:20:37.912
I believe the charges relate
to his climbing activities

00:20:38.019 --> 00:20:40.920
in the caves beneath
the planet's surface.

00:20:41.022 --> 00:20:44.788
This is the information
you requested, is it not?

00:20:44.826 --> 00:20:46.316
Thank you, Mr. Data.

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:07.848
What was your name again?

00:21:07.882 --> 00:21:09.281
Lieutenant Rhodes.

00:21:09.317 --> 00:21:13.253
Actually...
I meant your first name.

00:21:13.287 --> 00:21:14.879
Sandra.

00:21:14.922 --> 00:21:21.885
Well, Sandra, do you think you
could... give me some room?

00:21:21.929 --> 00:21:25.365
We're supposed to be
keeping an eye on you.

00:21:25.399 --> 00:21:28.163
Can't you keep an eye on me
from over there?

00:21:43.084 --> 00:21:44.551
Good morning.

00:21:44.585 --> 00:21:46.052
I thought you said

00:21:46.087 --> 00:21:49.545
your ship was the safest
place I could be.

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:51.080
Why the guards?

00:21:52.593 --> 00:21:56.085
Because Bok appeared
in my quarters last night.

00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:58.098
Now, it might not have been him.

00:21:58.132 --> 00:22:00.100
It may have been an image.

00:22:00.134 --> 00:22:01.601
We're investigating.

00:22:01.636 --> 00:22:04.730
Look, why don't you just
drop me off somewhere?

00:22:04.772 --> 00:22:06.740
I can watch out for myself.

00:22:06.774 --> 00:22:08.241
That wouldn't be wise.

00:22:08.276 --> 00:22:10.744
I've been doing it
since I was 15.

00:22:10.778 --> 00:22:13.679
I'm sure you have, but Bok
is a dangerous creature.

00:22:13.714 --> 00:22:15.079
He has a starship.

00:22:15.116 --> 00:22:16.583
He has technology.

00:22:16.617 --> 00:22:18.084
All right, all right.

00:22:18.119 --> 00:22:20.087
I'll stay here.

00:22:28.729 --> 00:22:31.197
You seem to like rock climbing.

00:22:31.232 --> 00:22:34.531
The holodeck can create
some very challenging climbs.

00:22:37.872 --> 00:22:38.998
We could go down together

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:41.008
and I can show you
how to use the program.

00:22:41.042 --> 00:22:43.602
Thanks, but, uh, I think
I can figure it out myself.

00:22:43.644 --> 00:22:45.236
Perhaps we could climb together.

00:22:45.279 --> 00:22:48.737
I'm probably not as...
skilled as you

00:22:48.783 --> 00:22:50.774
but I'm not inexperienced.

00:22:50.818 --> 00:22:52.911
Look... I'm sorry.

00:22:52.987 --> 00:22:55.922
I appreciate
what you're trying to do

00:22:55.957 --> 00:22:58.357
but, Captain...

00:23:00.628 --> 00:23:01.856
Captain?

00:23:01.896 --> 00:23:02.863
Father?

00:23:02.897 --> 00:23:03.864
Jean-Luc?

00:23:03.931 --> 00:23:05.865
I don't know
what I'm supposed to call you.

00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:08.562
As soon as this thing
with Bok is over

00:23:08.603 --> 00:23:10.230
I'm leaving.

00:23:10.271 --> 00:23:16.232
So, don't you see,
there really isn't any point

00:23:16.277 --> 00:23:18.711
in our getting acquainted.

00:23:23.084 --> 00:23:27.350
Let me know as soon
as you catch him, all right?

00:23:35.396 --> 00:23:39.264
Captain's Log, Stardate 47829.1.

00:23:39.300 --> 00:23:43.259
We've been in the Xendi Sabu
system for over three hours

00:23:43.304 --> 00:23:46.034
and still no sign of Bok.

00:23:46.073 --> 00:23:49.440
Captain, I am detecting
an object 5,000 kilometers

00:23:49.477 --> 00:23:50.910
off our starboard bow.

00:23:50.978 --> 00:23:52.445
It is another probe.

00:23:52.480 --> 00:23:54.539
Why didn't we detect it before?

00:23:54.582 --> 00:23:56.243
It must have been cloaked, sir.

00:23:56.283 --> 00:23:57.511
It came out of nowhere.

00:23:57.551 --> 00:24:00.850
On screen.

00:24:03.924 --> 00:24:07.382
Is it another
holographic device?

00:24:07.428 --> 00:24:10.090
I do not believe so.

00:24:10.131 --> 00:24:11.598
Captain, the probe's systems
are overloading.

00:24:11.632 --> 00:24:14.032
Red Alert!
Shields up.

00:24:23.944 --> 00:24:25.411
Damage report.

00:24:25.446 --> 00:24:27.107
No damage, sir.

00:24:27.148 --> 00:24:29.844
Captain, I do not believe
it was meant as an attack

00:24:29.884 --> 00:24:31.613
but rather as a message.

00:24:31.652 --> 00:24:32.641
A message?

00:24:32.687 --> 00:24:34.314
Yes sir, in B'Zal,
a Ferengi code

00:24:34.355 --> 00:24:36.016
which uses alternating patterns

00:24:36.057 --> 00:24:38.025
of light and darkness.

00:24:38.059 --> 00:24:39.788
Can you translate it?

00:24:39.827 --> 00:24:42.489
I am attempting to do so.

00:24:42.530 --> 00:24:44.498
The message reads

00:24:44.532 --> 00:24:47.797
"My revenge is at hand."

00:24:49.336 --> 00:24:53.830
He's proved that he can
get to us whenever he wants.

00:24:53.874 --> 00:24:56.365
Why doesn't he do something?

00:25:13.327 --> 00:25:15.795
Tea, Earl Grey, hot.

00:25:22.803 --> 00:25:24.566
If you want me to stay and talk

00:25:24.605 --> 00:25:27.096
you better not call
for security this time.

00:25:29.076 --> 00:25:31.271
How do you like your boy,
Captain?

00:25:31.312 --> 00:25:34.145
Is he everything
you'd always hoped for?

00:25:34.181 --> 00:25:36.581
It's a risky game
you're playing, coming here.

00:25:36.617 --> 00:25:38.778
Next time,
we'll be ready for you.

00:25:38.819 --> 00:25:40.286
Why don't we settle this now?

00:25:40.321 --> 00:25:44.348
Oh... and how do you
propose to do that, Picard?

00:25:44.391 --> 00:25:46.382
You murdered my son!

00:25:46.427 --> 00:25:48.759
It was self-defense...
he fired on my ship.

00:25:48.796 --> 00:25:50.764
You were in Ferengi space!

00:25:50.798 --> 00:25:52.265
I didn't know that.

00:25:52.299 --> 00:25:55.268
If he'd told me,
I would have withdrawn.

00:25:55.302 --> 00:25:59.238
I'm sorry, but there's nothing
I can do to bring him back.

00:25:59.273 --> 00:26:00.706
How touching.

00:26:00.741 --> 00:26:03.141
Your apology is worthless to me.

00:26:03.177 --> 00:26:06.613
I demand that you repay me
for my loss.

00:26:06.647 --> 00:26:09.275
You cannot put a price
on a life.

00:26:09.316 --> 00:26:11.284
Oh, but you can, Picard.

00:26:11.318 --> 00:26:14.412
You can pay me
with your son's life.

00:26:14.455 --> 00:26:15.717
No.

00:26:15.756 --> 00:26:17.121
You don't have any choice!

00:26:18.759 --> 00:26:22.320
I insist on being paid.

00:26:29.270 --> 00:26:30.737
That should do it.

00:26:30.771 --> 00:26:33.740
Let's run a level-3 bio-scan
just to be sure.

00:26:33.774 --> 00:26:35.605
Rhodes to Sick Bay.

00:26:35.643 --> 00:26:38.373
Medical emergency,
deck nine, section four.

00:26:38.412 --> 00:26:39.879
Let's go.

00:27:02.003 --> 00:27:05.302
Have you had any other seizures
like this before?

00:27:05.339 --> 00:27:06.636
No, not really.

00:27:06.674 --> 00:27:09.643
Sometimes my hand shakes,
but never this bad.

00:27:09.677 --> 00:27:12.373
When did it first
start to happen?

00:27:12.413 --> 00:27:14.108
About a few months ago.

00:27:14.148 --> 00:27:18.209
Do you have any idea
what's wrong with me?

00:27:18.252 --> 00:27:21.551
You have a condition called
the Forrester-Trent syndrome.

00:27:21.589 --> 00:27:23.716
It's a degenerative
neurological disorder...

00:27:23.758 --> 00:27:24.816
very rare.

00:27:24.859 --> 00:27:26.724
What do you mean, degenerative?

00:27:26.761 --> 00:27:28.228
If it goes untreated

00:27:28.262 --> 00:27:30.423
it could result in paralysis,
even death.

00:27:30.465 --> 00:27:32.194
I'm going to start you

00:27:32.233 --> 00:27:34.861
on a neuro-stabilization
regimen.

00:27:34.936 --> 00:27:38.064
If we're lucky,
it will halt the degeneration

00:27:38.105 --> 00:27:40.164
and maybe reverse its effects.

00:27:40.208 --> 00:27:42.005
The disease is hereditary.

00:27:42.043 --> 00:27:44.136
I know your father
doesn't have it.

00:27:44.178 --> 00:27:46.874
Was your mother prone
to these seizures?

00:27:46.914 --> 00:27:48.211
Not that I know of.

00:27:48.249 --> 00:27:50.809
There have been
some cases reported

00:27:50.852 --> 00:27:52.877
where the disease
was instigated

00:27:52.987 --> 00:27:54.454
by a random mutation.

00:27:54.489 --> 00:27:58.687
I'll run a micro-cellular scan
and see if that's what happened.

00:27:58.726 --> 00:28:02.059
In the meantime, I want you
to try to take it easy

00:28:02.096 --> 00:28:03.393
and get some rest.

00:28:12.373 --> 00:28:13.840
Is he going to be all right?

00:28:13.941 --> 00:28:16.102
I wish I could say for certain

00:28:16.143 --> 00:28:19.635
but I'm not sure how he'll
respond to treatments.

00:28:19.680 --> 00:28:23.582
I've been thinking about
what you said the other day

00:28:23.618 --> 00:28:27.520
and, you know,
I think you were right.

00:28:27.555 --> 00:28:28.852
I had convinced myself

00:28:28.923 --> 00:28:31.721
that Jason didn't want me
to reach out to him.

00:28:31.759 --> 00:28:34.319
You know, I don't think
anyone is born

00:28:34.362 --> 00:28:36.227
knowing how to be a parent.

00:28:36.264 --> 00:28:38.664
You just sort of figure it out
as you go

00:28:38.699 --> 00:28:41.998
but the one quality
that tends to be

00:28:42.036 --> 00:28:44.504
a requirement
for parenthood is patience.

00:28:44.539 --> 00:28:49.670
Well, I'm not sure
that that is going to be enough.

00:28:49.710 --> 00:28:51.644
I found out that...

00:28:51.679 --> 00:28:54.546
Jason has a criminal record.

00:28:54.582 --> 00:28:56.049
It's nothing very serious.

00:28:56.083 --> 00:28:57.482
It's only petty theft

00:28:57.518 --> 00:29:00.385
and so forth,
but I can't help feeling

00:29:00.421 --> 00:29:03.117
that if I had been
part of his life

00:29:03.157 --> 00:29:05.785
then he wouldn't be
so troubled now.

00:29:05.826 --> 00:29:07.589
Maybe, but why waste time

00:29:07.628 --> 00:29:10.256
blaming yourself
for not being there?

00:29:10.298 --> 00:29:12.095
Just be here for him now.

00:29:12.133 --> 00:29:14.226
And be patient?

00:29:14.268 --> 00:29:17.533
And be patient.

00:29:22.910 --> 00:29:25.310
We think we've found
something, Captain.

00:29:25.346 --> 00:29:28.042
Bok was in direct contact
with this chair

00:29:28.082 --> 00:29:29.606
for an extended period.

00:29:29.650 --> 00:29:33.552
It is showing a distinctive
subspace signature as a result.

00:29:33.588 --> 00:29:37.115
We think he's using some kind
of subspace transporter

00:29:37.158 --> 00:29:39.149
to beam aboard the Enterprise.

00:29:39.193 --> 00:29:42.856
My understanding is that
such devices were impractical.

00:29:42.964 --> 00:29:45.398
The Federation abandoned
its research in the field

00:29:45.433 --> 00:29:47.765
because the technology was
found to be unreliable

00:29:47.802 --> 00:29:49.133
as well as energy intensive.

00:29:49.170 --> 00:29:51.297
In order to transport matter
through subspace

00:29:51.339 --> 00:29:53.569
you have to put it
in a state of quantum flux.

00:29:53.608 --> 00:29:54.836
It's very unstable.

00:29:54.875 --> 00:29:56.968
What range would that kind
of transporter have?

00:29:57.011 --> 00:30:00.003
In theory, it could operate
over several light-years.

00:30:00.047 --> 00:30:01.844
That means that the probe
that exploded

00:30:01.882 --> 00:30:03.543
could have been beamed
into position

00:30:03.584 --> 00:30:05.745
from some point
outside sensor range.

00:30:05.786 --> 00:30:07.754
If Bok uses
his transporter again

00:30:07.788 --> 00:30:10.279
we might be able to trace
the subspace signature

00:30:10.324 --> 00:30:11.621
and locate his ship.

00:30:11.659 --> 00:30:13.684
Is there any way
we can we keep Bok

00:30:13.728 --> 00:30:16.196
from beaming aboard
the Enterprise again?

00:30:16.230 --> 00:30:18.664
I don't think there is.

00:30:18.699 --> 00:30:21.429
See, if he has the ability
to beam aboard

00:30:21.469 --> 00:30:23.903
he may be able
to beam someone away.

00:30:23.938 --> 00:30:26.133
It is a possibility.

00:30:26.173 --> 00:30:28.573
I'm concerned that he may try
to take Jason.

00:30:28.609 --> 00:30:30.577
Is there any way
we can protect him?

00:30:30.611 --> 00:30:31.908
You know, we might be able

00:30:31.946 --> 00:30:34.005
to keep a signal lock on him
at all times.

00:30:34.048 --> 00:30:35.515
If Bok tries to beam him away

00:30:35.549 --> 00:30:37.244
we might be able
to hold him here.

00:30:37.284 --> 00:30:38.512
In order to do so

00:30:38.552 --> 00:30:41.180
we would need to tie
the ship's subspace field coils

00:30:41.222 --> 00:30:42.655
into the transporter system.

00:30:42.690 --> 00:30:44.715
Make it so.

00:30:46.293 --> 00:30:51.253
Computer, where is Jason Vigo?

00:30:51.298 --> 00:30:54.426
Jason Vigo is in Holodeck Four.

00:31:20.261 --> 00:31:22.593
Would you wait outside?

00:32:12.213 --> 00:32:13.510
Not bad.

00:32:13.547 --> 00:32:16.243
I like climbing.

00:32:18.185 --> 00:32:20.483
There's something about

00:32:20.521 --> 00:32:24.355
actually having your fate
in your own hands.

00:32:24.391 --> 00:32:26.188
Yeah, I know.

00:32:26.227 --> 00:32:30.186
It looks as though
we may have found out

00:32:30.231 --> 00:32:32.756
how to locate Bok's ship.

00:32:32.800 --> 00:32:34.768
This could all soon be over.

00:32:34.802 --> 00:32:38.033
You came all the way up
here just to tell me that?

00:32:38.072 --> 00:32:40.165
I thought it would
make you feel better.

00:32:42.076 --> 00:32:43.134
Thanks.

00:32:43.177 --> 00:32:46.510
That was nice of you.

00:32:49.750 --> 00:32:52.719
Jason, when your mother
and I parted

00:32:52.753 --> 00:32:55.221
I lost track of her completely

00:32:55.256 --> 00:32:59.056
but I would like to know more
about what happened to her

00:32:59.093 --> 00:33:01.061
if you wouldn't mind telling me.

00:33:01.095 --> 00:33:02.062
Like what?

00:33:02.096 --> 00:33:04.496
Well, how did you end up
on Camor?

00:33:04.532 --> 00:33:07.865
It's an unlikely place
for a woman and child.

00:33:07.902 --> 00:33:09.699
Well, you know how she was...

00:33:09.737 --> 00:33:11.398
see a stray cat, take it in

00:33:11.438 --> 00:33:13.872
see somebody cold,
give them your coat.

00:33:13.941 --> 00:33:18.105
Yes, that was Miranda,
all right.

00:33:18.145 --> 00:33:20.579
She'd heard
about all the children

00:33:20.614 --> 00:33:24.778
that had been orphaned on Camor
from the Cardassian war.

00:33:24.819 --> 00:33:25.786
Oh... I see.

00:33:25.820 --> 00:33:28.288
I was only ten
when we went there.

00:33:28.322 --> 00:33:32.281
I remember her telling me
all about the boys and girls

00:33:32.326 --> 00:33:35.352
that didn't have anyone
to care for them.

00:33:37.798 --> 00:33:42.326
So she got this big house,
practically falling apart

00:33:42.369 --> 00:33:45.304
then she started
rounding up children.

00:33:45.339 --> 00:33:48.604
Eventually, there were
over 40 of us there.

00:33:50.611 --> 00:33:53.079
She called it a school.

00:33:53.113 --> 00:33:57.607
You know, she got up
before dawn every day

00:33:57.651 --> 00:34:01.451
and went to bed
well after midnight.

00:34:01.488 --> 00:34:05.515
In between, she never
stopped working.

00:34:07.394 --> 00:34:11.421
She taught us all how to read

00:34:11.465 --> 00:34:17.870
and she grew vegetables
in hardpan to feed us

00:34:17.905 --> 00:34:21.102
and she made sure
we knew how to sing.

00:34:21.141 --> 00:34:24.338
It's important
in a place like Camor.

00:34:27.047 --> 00:34:30.380
And then one day
she was attacked

00:34:30.417 --> 00:34:34.717
by two men in the street
in broad daylight

00:34:34.755 --> 00:34:38.555
for the food she was carrying

00:34:38.592 --> 00:34:40.992
and if she'd just
given it to them

00:34:41.028 --> 00:34:43.496
they probably
wouldn't have hurt her

00:34:43.530 --> 00:34:47.523
but she knew how important
the food was to us.

00:34:50.237 --> 00:34:52.000
So they killed her.

00:34:53.908 --> 00:34:55.808
I'm so sorry.

00:34:57.211 --> 00:34:59.179
Don't be sorry for me.

00:34:59.213 --> 00:35:00.908
My mother made sure

00:35:01.015 --> 00:35:04.451
that we were all
tough enough to make it.

00:35:04.485 --> 00:35:09.821
Jason, isn't there some way
that I can be a father to you?

00:35:09.857 --> 00:35:12.621
My own father and I
were estranged.

00:35:12.660 --> 00:35:16.858
He wanted me to stay at home
and tend the vineyards

00:35:16.931 --> 00:35:20.731
and I wanted to join Starfleet.

00:35:20.768 --> 00:35:25.865
And he died before we could
come to terms with that

00:35:25.973 --> 00:35:30.342
and I've regretted that
all of my life.

00:35:30.377 --> 00:35:35.679
I don't want the same thing
to happen to you and me.

00:35:35.716 --> 00:35:37.741
You don't understand.

00:35:37.785 --> 00:35:40.515
I'm not anybody
you'd want for a son.

00:35:40.554 --> 00:35:42.715
Trust me, if you knew...

00:35:42.756 --> 00:35:44.189
if you knew anything about me

00:35:44.224 --> 00:35:46.556
you wouldn't,
you wouldn't be trying so hard.

00:35:46.593 --> 00:35:48.117
You're so wrong.

00:35:48.162 --> 00:35:49.220
Oh, really?

00:35:49.263 --> 00:35:51.254
Let me spell it out for you.

00:35:51.298 --> 00:35:54.426
I've been in trouble
since I was a teenager.

00:35:54.468 --> 00:35:55.435
I lie.

00:35:55.469 --> 00:35:57.869
I steal.

00:35:57.905 --> 00:35:59.338
I use people.

00:35:59.373 --> 00:36:01.034
I'm a criminal.

00:36:01.075 --> 00:36:03.805
That's what your son is.

00:36:03.844 --> 00:36:06.074
I know.

00:36:06.113 --> 00:36:08.445
You do?

00:36:08.482 --> 00:36:09.847
Oh, yes.

00:36:09.950 --> 00:36:13.386
I know all about your troubles
with the Camor authorities.

00:36:14.688 --> 00:36:15.985
You do?

00:36:16.023 --> 00:36:18.423
It doesn't make
any difference, Jason.

00:36:18.459 --> 00:36:20.654
You're still my son

00:36:20.694 --> 00:36:24.528
and like it or not,
I'm your father.

00:36:27.001 --> 00:36:29.868
I don't know what that means.

00:36:29.903 --> 00:36:32.872
I know it means something.

00:36:32.906 --> 00:36:35.670
There's some connection.

00:36:37.177 --> 00:36:38.644
Yeah.

00:36:38.679 --> 00:36:41.170
But one thing is clear...

00:36:41.215 --> 00:36:43.877
you'll never look
at your hairline again

00:36:43.951 --> 00:36:45.441
in the same way.

00:37:01.001 --> 00:37:02.832
You wanted to see me?

00:37:02.936 --> 00:37:03.834
Yes.

00:37:03.937 --> 00:37:05.996
It's about Jason.

00:37:11.545 --> 00:37:13.513
I finished

00:37:13.547 --> 00:37:16.948
the micro-cellular scan
I was running.

00:37:16.984 --> 00:37:19.953
There's something
you need to know.

00:37:19.987 --> 00:37:21.511
Sir, sensors are detecting

00:37:21.555 --> 00:37:24.149
a subspace carrier wave
headed for the ship.

00:37:24.191 --> 00:37:27.217
Its signature is consistent
with Bok's transporter.

00:37:27.261 --> 00:37:29.991
See if you can trace it
and locate Bok's ship.

00:37:30.030 --> 00:37:31.964
Geordi, are you ready
down there?

00:37:31.999 --> 00:37:33.864
I've got a signal lock on Jason.

00:37:33.967 --> 00:37:35.400
Riker to Picard.

00:37:35.436 --> 00:37:36.869
Picard here.

00:37:36.970 --> 00:37:39.564
Bok is trying
to use his transporter.

00:37:44.912 --> 00:37:50.009
The transporter beam is focusing
on deck nine, section four.

00:37:50.050 --> 00:37:51.677
Jason's quarters.

00:37:51.718 --> 00:37:53.845
I'm on it, Commander.

00:37:53.887 --> 00:37:55.855
Security to Bridge.

00:37:55.889 --> 00:37:58.881
Bok is beaming Jason
off the ship.

00:38:00.227 --> 00:38:02.320
Initiating transport now.

00:38:09.169 --> 00:38:11.364
I'm losing his signal.

00:38:13.207 --> 00:38:16.574
Bok is reestablishing
his lock on him.

00:38:30.490 --> 00:38:32.685
Have you been able
to locate Bok's ship?

00:38:32.726 --> 00:38:33.750
No, sir.

00:38:33.793 --> 00:38:35.852
The subspace signature
left by his transporter

00:38:35.896 --> 00:38:37.693
is decaying more
rapidly than predicted.

00:38:37.731 --> 00:38:40.165
It may not be possible
to trace it.

00:38:40.200 --> 00:38:43.328
Captain, another probe
has materialized

00:38:43.370 --> 00:38:45.338
500 kilometers to starboard.

00:38:45.372 --> 00:38:47.465
It is sending a transmission.

00:38:47.507 --> 00:38:49.099
Put it on screen.

00:38:49.142 --> 00:38:53.511
This is
a very special day, Picard.

00:38:53.546 --> 00:38:57.573
15 years ago you took my son
away from me.

00:38:57.617 --> 00:39:01.576
Today, I will take your son
away from you.

00:39:01.621 --> 00:39:04.215
It will be our anniversary.

00:39:06.893 --> 00:39:10.954
I wanted you
to see him one last time.

00:39:14.034 --> 00:39:16.195
I am tracing
the transporter beam

00:39:16.236 --> 00:39:18.261
Bok used to send the probe.

00:39:18.305 --> 00:39:19.738
The ship is holding position

00:39:19.773 --> 00:39:21.468
approximately
300 billion kilometers

00:39:21.508 --> 00:39:22.770
from here.

00:39:22.809 --> 00:39:24.003
Plot a course.

00:39:24.044 --> 00:39:25.534
Maximum warp.

00:39:26.813 --> 00:39:28.804
Even at warp nine,
we wouldn't get there

00:39:28.848 --> 00:39:30.042
for another 20 minutes.

00:39:30.083 --> 00:39:32.745
The modifications you made
to the transporter...

00:39:32.786 --> 00:39:36.586
is there any way we could use
a subspace transport from here

00:39:36.623 --> 00:39:38.352
to get me onto Bok's ship?

00:39:38.391 --> 00:39:41.224
It may be possible, sir,
but it would not be advisable.

00:39:41.261 --> 00:39:42.956
I'll take that as a yes.

00:39:42.996 --> 00:39:44.122
You're with me.

00:39:52.839 --> 00:39:54.272
There.

00:39:54.307 --> 00:39:56.605
I've aligned the field coils.

00:39:56.643 --> 00:39:58.611
Phase dampers are in sync.

00:39:58.645 --> 00:40:01.773
Standing by to modulate
the transport pattern.

00:40:01.815 --> 00:40:05.307
Captain, we might be able
to get you over there

00:40:05.352 --> 00:40:07.843
but I don't see how
we're going to get you back.

00:40:07.887 --> 00:40:09.946
We'll deal with that
when the time comes.

00:40:11.091 --> 00:40:12.888
Transport's going to take
longer than normal.

00:40:12.926 --> 00:40:14.188
We'll have to shunt
your pattern

00:40:14.227 --> 00:40:16.195
through the subspace
field coils.

00:40:16.229 --> 00:40:17.560
Understood.

00:40:17.597 --> 00:40:20.395
Initiating transport
sequence now.

00:40:22.502 --> 00:40:24.231
Maybe we can make a deal.

00:40:24.270 --> 00:40:25.897
What kind of deal?

00:40:25.939 --> 00:40:28.203
Tell my father you killed me.

00:40:28.241 --> 00:40:31.642
Put a phaser burn on my shirt
and send it to him.

00:40:31.678 --> 00:40:33.168
He'll think I'm dead.

00:40:33.213 --> 00:40:35.773
That's what this
is about, isn't it?

00:40:35.815 --> 00:40:37.908
I got friends on Camor V

00:40:37.984 --> 00:40:40.646
that will make it
worth your while.

00:40:40.687 --> 00:40:42.780
I understand your desire to live

00:40:42.822 --> 00:40:45.086
but I want Picard
to see your body

00:40:45.125 --> 00:40:46.854
so there will be no doubt.

00:40:48.661 --> 00:40:52.119
Lower your weapons
or Bok is dead.

00:40:54.167 --> 00:40:56.226
Lower yours or your son dies!

00:40:56.269 --> 00:40:59.727
You know as well as I do, Bok,
he's not my son.

00:40:59.773 --> 00:41:01.934
I know what you've done.

00:41:01.975 --> 00:41:05.035
Miranda Vigo is his mother

00:41:05.078 --> 00:41:06.636
but I am not his father.

00:41:06.679 --> 00:41:08.044
You made it appear so

00:41:08.081 --> 00:41:10.072
because you
re-sequenced his DNA

00:41:10.116 --> 00:41:12.516
but your technique was flawed.

00:41:12.552 --> 00:41:15.487
He developed
a neurological disorder.

00:41:15.522 --> 00:41:18.457
When my ship's doctor
investigated it

00:41:18.491 --> 00:41:21.085
she discovered
what you had done.

00:41:21.127 --> 00:41:24.290
Now he'll never pay the ransom.

00:41:24.330 --> 00:41:25.490
Shut up!

00:41:25.532 --> 00:41:26.760
There never was a ransom.

00:41:26.800 --> 00:41:29.030
All he was ever interested in
was vengeance.

00:41:30.437 --> 00:41:32.735
DaiMon, is this true?

00:41:32.772 --> 00:41:34.569
He's not a DaiMon!

00:41:34.607 --> 00:41:36.404
He was stripped of command.

00:41:36.443 --> 00:41:39.071
They had no right
to do that to me.

00:41:39.112 --> 00:41:42.513
He lied to you, so that you
would help him in his plan.

00:41:42.549 --> 00:41:45.382
The Enterprise is closing in
on your position.

00:41:45.418 --> 00:41:48.512
If you let the two of us go,
they won't attack you.

00:41:48.555 --> 00:41:50.921
They won't attack us
with you on board.

00:41:51.024 --> 00:41:54.221
They will cripple your ship
and keep you here

00:41:54.260 --> 00:41:57.559
until the Ferengi
authorities arrive.

00:41:57.597 --> 00:42:00.065
You've got
a lot of explaining to do.

00:42:00.100 --> 00:42:03.092
Your only hope
is to turn Bok over to them

00:42:03.136 --> 00:42:05.502
and tell them
that he deceived you.

00:42:13.746 --> 00:42:17.045
There is no profit
in this for us.

00:42:24.691 --> 00:42:27.626
Captain's Log, Stardate 47831.8.

00:42:27.660 --> 00:42:29.287
At Jason's request

00:42:29.329 --> 00:42:32.662
the Enterprise has returned
to Camor V.

00:42:32.699 --> 00:42:33.893
Dr. Crusher feels

00:42:33.933 --> 00:42:36.561
I'm responding well
to the treatment.

00:42:36.603 --> 00:42:40.300
She thinks that the damage
may be completely reversed.

00:42:40.340 --> 00:42:41.637
I'm glad to hear it.

00:42:41.674 --> 00:42:42.663
Yeah.

00:42:42.709 --> 00:42:44.336
Are you sure that you
wouldn't like to stay

00:42:44.377 --> 00:42:46.106
on board the Enterprise
for a few more days?

00:42:46.146 --> 00:42:47.306
Uh, I can't.

00:42:47.347 --> 00:42:49.315
I have a life back on Camor.

00:42:49.349 --> 00:42:52.182
It's a mess,
but I'd like to go back

00:42:52.218 --> 00:42:53.480
and straighten things out.

00:42:53.520 --> 00:42:54.851
I understand.

00:43:00.660 --> 00:43:04.756
Well, uh, maybe next time
you come back this way

00:43:04.797 --> 00:43:06.458
you can look me up.

00:43:06.499 --> 00:43:07.796
I will.

00:43:07.834 --> 00:43:09.995
I, uh, put a little something

00:43:10.036 --> 00:43:12.869
into your bag
while you were packing.

00:43:20.480 --> 00:43:23.074
I know you would
probably have preferred

00:43:23.116 --> 00:43:24.845
a bottle of Saurian brandy

00:43:24.884 --> 00:43:27.250
but, uh, that's all
I could come up with.

00:43:27.287 --> 00:43:29.312
I-I can't accept this.

00:43:29.355 --> 00:43:31.915
I want you to have it.

00:43:53.213 --> 00:43:55.807
Energize.
